            <ArticleTitle>Dual-catheter covered stenting: a novel approach to the treatment of large coronary artery perforations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>348-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary perforation is an infrequent but potentially devastating complication of coronary intervention. Treatment of a broad-based perforation usually requires emergent pericardiocentesis and thoracotomy. We present a novel approach to closure of &gt; or = 1 mm diameter perforations using a dual-catheter covered stent technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
